1. hitl.py:
   - PendingAction (frozen dataclass): id ("ACT-xxxx"), bundle_id, tool in {"create_report","add_line","submit_report"}, payload (deep-copied dict, wrap in MappingProxyType or deep-freeze so it cannot be mutated), payload_hash = sha256(json.dumps(payload, sort_keys=True, separators=(",",":"))), created_at (UTC iso), employee_id (owner), status field kept in a separate mutable record so the payload itself stays immutable.
   - Bundle record: bundle_id ("BND-xxxx"), employee_id, run_id, status (pending|approved|rejected|superseded|executed|failed), action ids, lines (ExpenseLine data + flags + justification), supersedes (optional), created_at, bundle_hash (sha256 over the ordered action hashes plus justifications). One pending bundle per session at a time; staging a new bundle supersedes any older pending one.
   - stage_write_tool(tool, args, ctx) is the ONLY function write tools call: it validates args (S3 check_line for add_line, using staged lines of the same bundle for the daily meal total), returns the standard error shape on any error or block flag (nothing stored), requires create_report to be staged before add_line and add_line before submit_report (BAD_BUNDLE otherwise), uses the placeholder report_ref "$REPORT" in add_line/submit payloads, stores a PendingAction, logs pending_created, and returns {"ok":True,"queued":True,"action_id":..., "message":"Queued for the user's approval. Nothing has been filed."}. It must never import or call mock_api write functions.
   - build_bundle_view(bundle) -> the Bundle JSON from the Shared Context (lines with flags, requires_justification, total_amount, each action with payload_hash, and the bundle_hash as "payload_hash" for the approve call).
   - approve(bundle_id, employee_id, client_hash, justifications) -> result. Steps in this exact order, each failure returns the standard error shape and logs a guardrail_block + hitl_decision: (1) bundle exists (NOT_FOUND) and belongs to employee (FORBIDDEN); (2) status == pending (ACTION_NOT_PENDING); (3) recompute the bundle hash from stored actions and compare to BOTH the stored bundle_hash and client_hash (PAYLOAD_HASH_MISMATCH); (4) apply any user-typed justifications to lines that have an OVER_LIMIT exception flag, re-hash and require a non-empty justification (min 5 chars after strip) for every exception line (JUSTIFICATION_REQUIRED). Justification is stored on the line and included in the hash. NOTE: the justification text is entered at approve time, but the client_hash was computed over the line WITHOUT the justification, so define the hash input as the actions only and track justifications separately but record them in the log. (5) set status approved; for each action in order call gate.issue(action_id) and then the mock_api write function with the token, substituting "$REPORT" with the real report id from step 1 and injecting employee_id from the bundle owner (never from the payload); stop at the first API error, mark the bundle failed, and return exactly what was and was not written. (6) mark executed; return {"ok":True,"report_id":..., "lines_added": n, "status":"submitted","message": built in code}. A second approve call on the same bundle must return ACTION_NOT_PENDING and write nothing.
