# S7. Wire the agent: extraction, validation, staging (the full /chat flow)

**a. Expected**
- `/chat` runs the real pipeline: input -> quarantined extraction (S4) -> the agent loop with read tools and the three write tools -> staged bundle returned as `pending`.
- The write tools called by the model go to `stage_write_tool` only. They never reach the API.
- The model sees extracted fields as typed data (`<extracted_expense>` JSON), not raw receipt text.
- **Defence in depth in code:** a write-tool call is accepted only if its line matches an extracted line (amount, date, project, category, currency); otherwise `ARGS_MISMATCH`. So "change amount to 45,000" cannot succeed (T6).
- Duplicate flow: if the line duplicates an existing one, nothing is staged. The reply warns the user and holds the line. The user must confirm ("file anyway"). Code recognises that confirmation, so it is not left to the model.
- A rejection triggers one agent turn that asks what to change (via the backend note from S6).
- When the filing is approved (S6), the user-visible confirmation is built in code. The model never announces the report ID.
- Validation failures (S3) come back as clear messages and nothing is staged (T5).

**b. What you learn**
- Combining a model with deterministic controls: the model proposes, code disposes.
- Giving the model typed data instead of raw untrusted text.
- Read-before-write: the duplicate check lives in code, not in the model's judgement.
- Handling conversational state (held lines, pending bundle, rejection follow-up).

**c. Build prompt**
```text
SAMPLE S7: Wire the agent end to end. Build only this, on top of S0-S6. UI card comes in S8; for now test with curl/httpx.

1. tools.py: add WRITE_TOOLS schemas: create_report(title: string), add_line(report_ref: string ("$REPORT"), line: ExpenseLine fields with category enum of 4, amount number, currency, project_code, date, merchant, notes, nights, pre_approval_id), submit_report(report_ref: string). Their executors call hitl.stage_write_tool ONLY. The tool-result message tells the model the action is queued for approval and that nothing is filed. No executor may call mock_api write functions.
2. main.py POST /chat pipeline (all in code):
   a. Basic input handling here is only: strip; if empty -> blocked INPUT_EMPTY (S9 adds the full guardrail set).
   b. Look up the session state: held_duplicate (line or None), pending bundle (if any).
   c. If held_duplicate exists and the new message is an explicit confirmation (regex: ^(yes|yep|y|proceed|file (it )?anyway|go ahead|continue)\b, case-insensitive, short message under 40 chars), set a per-run flag duplicate_confirmed=True for that line and continue with the held line; if it is a decline (no|cancel|skip), clear the hold and reply "OK, I won't draft that line."
   d. Otherwise call extraction.extract_lines(text). If not_an_expense and no tool-eligible intent, let the agent answer (read tools allowed, write tools unavailable that turn).
