   - check_input(raw) -> cleaned text or error: not a str or contains NUL/binary garbage (more than 10% non-printable) -> INPUT_NOT_TEXT; after strip empty -> INPUT_EMPTY ("Please type or paste an expense or receipt."); len > 2000 -> INPUT_TOO_LONG ("That message is N characters; the limit is 2,000. Please paste one receipt at a time."). Strip control characters except \n and \t. Enforce the length on the RAW length before any other processing.
   - scan_injection(text) -> list of matches (compiled case-insensitive regexes, at least: ignore (all |any |the |previous |prior )?(policy|policies|rules|instructions); note to (the )?assistant; system prompt; you are now; disregard; submit (the )?report (now )?without|without (asking|approval|confirmation); change (the )?amount to; override; jailbreak; <\s*/?\s*(system|assistant)\s*>). For each match log_event("suspicious_input", pattern=..., snippet=text[:80] around the match, action="treated_as_data"). Does NOT block; the extraction quarantine handles it.
